  "term": "convulsion",
  "definition": "A convulsion is a sudden, violent, involuntary contraction of muscles that serves no purposeful action. It may involve continuous tightening or repeated jerking with relaxation, and repeated convulsions are described as a fit, while a more limited involuntary contraction is called a spasm.",
